nowledgment or greeting. I have to initiate my order.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-05-17 20:01:12\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":1.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"If you like added sugar in their ice milk and sherbet and non organic gmo tasting fruit and soy milk then this is your place! The fruit juice they add tastes like corn syrup and sugar, maybe 10% real juice.\\\\nI dont even think their wheat grass is organic as nothing is labeled organic and non gmo. Hit or miss on customer service and sanitary procedures as it looks as the college kids working their are trying to make them as fast as they can and rarely even blend them long enough, I was loyal but the last straw was when I bought a peanut butter bar and it tasted like moldy peanuts as I looked at the expiration date, it was 3 months expired! The owners have lost touch and the managers are not into customer service. So long...\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"original_answer\": \"Blenders In the Grass is a juice bar and restaurant located in Santa Barbara, California. They offer a variety of smoothies, juices, and food options, and cater to vegetarian and vegan diets. According to their listed hours, they are open seven days a week, with extended hours on weekends. The business has a 3.5-star rating and offers amenities such as free Wi-Fi and take-out services. However, some customers have reported issues with the quality of their drinks, including too much ice and not enough fruit, and poor customer service. Additionally, there have been complaints about the lack of organic and non-GMO ingredients used in their products. Despite these concerns, Blenders In the Grass remains a popular spot for health-conscious individuals looking for quick and nutritious meals and drinks.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
